title Every synth: each engine on Track 1, eight notes held, then a run, and the arp latched on Poly
covers load, note-repeat
# Track 1's instrument steps through every engine in the Synth options'
# Instrument row. On the MPC each engine's window measures what eight
# voices cost (the report's per-engine rows); the tests' session builds no
# instruments, so it checks the steps and leaves the sound to the MPC.
wait 1
tap header tab Synth
mark poly
button MENU
button +
button MENU
wait 1
expect-on-mpc track 1: plays Poly
pad-down 1 100
pad-down 5 100
pad-down 8 100
pad-down 10 100
pad-down 13 100
pad-down 15 100
pad-down 16 100
pad-down 12 100
wait 3
pad-up 1
pad-up 5
pad-up 8
pad-up 10
pad-up 13
pad-up 15
pad-up 16
pad-up 12
wait 0.5
pad 1 63 0.1
pad 2 66 0.1
pad 3 69 0.1
pad 4 72 0.1
pad 5 75 0.1
pad 6 78 0.1
pad 7 81 0.1
pad 8 84 0.1
pad 9 87 0.1
pad 10 90 0.1
pad 11 93 0.1
pad 12 96 0.1
pad 13 99 0.1
pad 14 102 0.1
pad 15 105 0.1
pad 16 108 0.1
wait 1
mark arp
button SHIFT + NOTE REPEAT
expect Latch on
pad-down 1 100
pad-down 5 100
pad-down 8 100
wait 0.5
pad-up 1
pad-up 5
pad-up 8
button PLAY
wait 4
button SHIFT + NOTE REPEAT
expect Latch off
button STOP
wait 1
mark fm
button MENU
button +
button MENU
wait 1
expect-on-mpc track 1: plays FM
